an3.52:5.1 starts: When one departs this life,
an3.52:5.2 starts: self-control over body, speech, and mind,
an3.52:5.3 starts: and the deeds of merit one did while
an3.52:5.4 starts: lead to one’s happiness.
an3.57:11.1 starts: who has gone beyond all things of the
an3.57:11.2 starts: and by non-clinging has reached nibbāna:
an3.57:11.3 starts: an offering is truly vast
an3.57:11.4 starts: when planted in that spotless field.
an3.57:12.1 starts: Fools devoid of understanding,
an3.57:12.2 starts: dull-witted, unlearned,
an3.57:12.3 starts: do not attend on the holy ones
an3.57:12.4 starts: but give their gifts to those outside.
an3.57:13.1 starts: Those, however, who attend on the holy ones,
an3.57:13.2 starts: on the wise ones esteemed as sagely,
an3.57:13.3 starts: and those whose faith in the Fortunate One
an3.57:13.4 starts: is deeply rooted and well established,
an3.58:9.1 starts: “the wise one, dispeller of darkness,
an3.58:9.2 starts: the triple-knowledge bearer, victor over death;
an3.58:9.3 starts: the one they call an abandoner of all,
an3.58:9.4 starts: benefactor of devas and humans;
an3.58:10.1 starts: “the one possessing the three knowledges,
an3.58:10.2 starts: who dwells without delusion;
an3.58:10.3 starts: they worship him, the Buddha
an3.58:10.4 starts: Gotama, bearing his final body.
an4.15:3.1 starts: In this world together with its devas
an4.15:3.2 starts: above, across, and below,
an4.15:3.3 starts: as far as the world extends,
an4.15:3.4 starts: the Buddha is declared foremost.
an4.21:10.1 starts: all those dwelled, now dwell,
an4.21:10.2 starts: and in the future will dwell
an4.21:10.3 starts: revering the good Dhamma.
an4.21:10.4 starts: This is the nature of the Buddhas.
an4.22:5.1 starts: The dullard with a restless mind
an4.22:5.2 starts: who speaks much chatter,
an4.22:5.3 starts: his thoughts unsettled,
an4.22:5.4 starts: delighting in a bad teaching,
an4.22:5.5 starts: holding bad views, disrespectful,
an4.22:5.6 starts: is far from an elder’s stature.
an4.24:8.1 starts: Amid those who are self-constrained, the Stable One
an4.24:8.2 starts: would not posit as categorically true or false
an4.24:8.3 starts: anything seen, heard, or sensed,
an4.24:8.4 starts: clung to and considered truth by others.
an4.25:2.1 starts: The Blessed One taught the spiritual life,
an4.25:2.2 starts: not based on tradition, culminating in nibbāna,
an4.25:2.3 starts: lived for the sake of
an4.25:2.4 starts: restraint and abandoning.
an4.25:2.5 starts: This is the path of the great beings,
an4.25:2.6 starts: the path followed by the great seers.
